From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:01:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] MdeModulePkg/UefiBootManagerLib: Fix short-form hard drive
 boot regression

PR #12829 added an early return when LocateHandleBuffer() failed
during short-form hard drive device path expansion. On a fast boot,
a miss in the HDDP cache can occur before Block I/O handles are
available, so the return bypassed EfiBootManagerConnectAll() and
prevented the fallback search from finding the device.

Continue with an empty handle list after the lookup failure. This lets
the existing path connect all controllers and retry the Block I/O search.

Signed-off-by: Michael D Kinney <michael.d.kinney@intel.com>

ouroBIOS backport of tianocore/edk2 commit 027e7a437 (merged on
2026-10-08, after edk2-stable202608, the base of MrChromebox's
uefipayload_2608), applied unchanged. Drop it when the base includes
it.

Why here: the early return came with "MdeModulePkg: Fix missing NULL
tests" (77cf8c8c1), which is in the base, and both boards boot their
OS from short-form hard drive device paths (the boot entries that
efibootmgr, shim and Windows create, kept in the HDDP variable), so a
miss of that cache before the Block I/O handles exist could skip the
entry instead of connecting the controllers and trying again.

TEST=git cherry-pick on the series: a clean merge at another offset
(MrChromebox's BmBoot.c moves it), the same seven lines as upstream.
No EDK2 build here.
---
 MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c
index 381716eceb..84baec2bb3 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Library/UefiBootManagerLib/BmBoot.c
@@ -1029,7 +1029,13 @@ BmExpandPartitionDevicePath (
 
     Status = gBS->LocateHandleBuffer (ByProtocol, &gEfiBlockIoProtocolGuid, NULL, &BlockIoHandleCount, &BlockIoBuffer);
     if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
-      return NULL;
+      //
+      // No Block I/O handles found.  Set count to 0 and buffer to NULL and
+      // continue to allow search for Block I/O handles to be tried again after
+      // attempting a ConnectAll.
+      //
+      BlockIoHandleCount = 0;
+      BlockIoBuffer      = NULL;
     }
 
     //
-- 
